ppen upon a  tabloid from 1959 in which victor creole  claims demons killed his loved ones  wanting to hear the truth straight from  the source nancy and robin disguise  themselves as psychology students and  request an interview with the now  elderly and imprisoned victor creel  his account seems to confirm the kid's  suspicions his family bought the big  blue house and were very happy there for  about a month then upsetting  supernatural phenomena started to occur  victor believes his home in hawkins was  haunted by a demon who tortured and  killed his wife virginia and daughter  alice while it kept him occupied with  nightmarish visions his son henry he  says was found in a coma and died days  later victor was so destroyed by what  the supposed demon had wrought that he  gouged his own eyes out and hopes it  would take him too he's a shell of a man  when nancy and robin come to question  him and as of yet he doesn't know the  real story of what happened  one of the more confusing elements of  stranger things 4 is all the various  uniformed agencies pursuing 11. after  jane hopper concusses the bully angel  over the skate the local police show up  at the buyer's house to take ellen to  custody meanwhile lieutenant colonel  sullivan arrives at dr owen's personal  residence in nevada he plays nice at  first but then he lets owens in on the  real reason for his surprise middle of  the night helicopter visit the us  military thinks the hawkins lab was  training kids like 11 to be remote  assassins and the suspect l not eddie  actually killed chrissy and fred owens  swears she's dead but sullivan ransacks  the house and intends to tail him if he  goes looking for 11. dr owens gets to l  first when his people intercept her on  her way to juvie sullivan's thugs aren't  far behind they open fire at the buyer's  house with little concern as to whether  the kids are collateral damage  sullivan himself later interrogates a  guard who survived the shootout to get  the underground lab's location when  episode 7 ends he has the information he  needs but so do mike will jonathan and  argyle who are all headed to the same  place on the map  jamie campbell bower is credited with  playing peter ballard on stranger things  but he's actually playing a kind of  quadruple role that serves as the fourth  season's big reveal  sometimes  papa doesn't tell the truth  eleven meets ballard in the memories she  revisits thanks to the nina machine  where he's a lowly lab assistant who  occasionally stands up for her ballard  earns her trust and promises to help her  escape but really he just needs l to  remove the device preventing him from  harnessing his powers that's because  ballard is the mythical one that dr  brenner claims doesn't exist  he not l committed the hawkins lap  massacre but that's not all one is also  henry the son of victor creel henry  seems to have demonstrated a proclivity  for evil since early in his childhood  since a family moved to hawkins to try  and rid him of his demons we know that  hawkins in the lab aren't specifically  tied to his predicament or the upside  down  the young henry creel resented his  parents for trying to make him conform  when they seek the help of a doctor he  kills his mom and sister in the same way  becna disposes of his victims and frames  his dad for their incomprehensibly  gruesome murders in the aftermath he  ends up confined to the hawkins lab  anyway where l used her powers to send  him into the upside down where he  transforms into this season's big bad  beckham this development ties up a lot  of loose ends from seasons one through  three but whether we call him peter  ballard one henry creel or vecna his  story isn't over yet  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

